\end{displaymath}
Due to the stiff well-posedness of \cref{eq}, there exists a 
constant $K_1 > 0$ such that 
\begin{displaymath}
  \|{\hat{u}(s, \xi, \eta)}\| \le K_1 \|{\hat{U}_0(\xi)}\|,
\end{displaymath}
for each $s \ge 0$, $\xi \in \mathbb{R}^d$ and $\eta \ge 0$. Therefore, 
\begin{multline*}
  \norm{ \big( \hat{u}(t, \cdot, \eta) - \exp(H_{11} t) \hat{u}_0
  \big) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} \\
  \le \norm{ G(t, \cdot, \eta) \hat{v}_0 
  \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} 
  + \int_0^t 
  \norm{ G(t-s, \cdot, \eta) H_{21} \hat{u}(s, \cdot, \eta)
  \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} \,\mathrm{d} s \\
  \le \sup_{s \in [0, t]} \sup_{|\xi| \le \Xi} \| G(s, \xi, \eta) \|
  \cdot \bigg( \| \hat{v}_0 \|_{L^2} + 
  t K_1 \sup_{|\xi| \le \Xi} \| H_{21}(\xi, 0) \| \cdot
  \| \hat{U}_0 \|_{L^2} \bigg),
\end{multline*}
which yields the desired convergence.

Let us now consider the case when the matrix sets $\mathcal{F}_1$ and 
$\mathcal{F}_2$ are uniformly quasi-stable.
Note that 
