  \big) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| > \Xi} }_{L^2} 
  < \frac{1}{2} \mu,
\end{displaymath}
according to \Cref{lemma:high_frequency}. 
By \Cref{lemma:low_frequency}, there exists a constant 
$\Theta > 0$ such that the following inequality holds for each 
$\eta > \Theta$:
\begin{displaymath}
  \norm{ \big( \hat{u}(t, \cdot, \eta) - \exp(H_{11} t) \hat{u}_0
  \big) \mathbbm{1}_{|\cdot| \le \Xi} }_{L^2} 
