At this time, one can obtain that 
\begin{displaymath}
  \norm{ \big( \hat{u}(t, \cdot, \eta) - \exp(H_{11} t) \hat{u}_0
  \big) }_{L^2} < \mu,
\end{displaymath}
which yields the desired convergence.

Furthermore, if the matrix set $\mathcal{F}_2$ is uniformly quasi-stable 
and the initial data satisfies $U_0 \in H^2$, then the 
error estimate at the low-frequency region with the frequency 
